'''''Serapias cordigera''''' is a species of [[orchid]]s found from the [[Azores]], south-central [[Europe]] to the [[Mediterranean]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Giuseppe Pellegrino |last2=Francesca Bellusci |date=2014 |title=Effects of human disturbance on reproductive success and population viability of Serapias cordigera (Orchidaceae) |url=https://search.nal.usda.gov/discovery/search?query=lds35,contains,823593-01nal_inst,AND&tab=LibraryCatalog&search_scope=MyInstitution&vid=01NAL_INST:MAIN&mode=advanced&offset=0 |journal=Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society |language=English |volume=176 |issue=3 |pages=408–420 |doi=10.1111/boj.12204 |s2cid=82784486 |issn=0024-4074|doi-access=free }}</ref>

